NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000022 "#"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000023 "#    For brief instructions, try 'perltidy -h'."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000024 "#    For more complete documentation, try 'man perltidy'"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000025 "#    or visit the GitHub site https://perltidy.github.io/perltidy/"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000026 "#"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000027 "#    This script is an example of the default style.  It was formatted with:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000028 "#"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000029 "#      perltidy Tidy.pm"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000030 "#"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000031 "#    Code Contributions: See ChangeLog.html for a complete history."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000032 "#      Michael Cartmell supplied code for adaptation to VMS and helped with"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000033 "#        v-strings."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000034 "#      Hugh S. Myers supplied sub streamhandle and the supporting code to"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000035 "#        create a Perl::Tidy module which can operate on strings, arrays, etc."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000036 "#      Yves Orton supplied coding to help detect Windows versions."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000037 "#      Axel Rose supplied a patch for MacPerl."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000038 "#      Sebastien Aperghis-Tramoni supplied a patch for the defined or operator."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000039 "#      Dan Tyrell contributed a patch for binary I/O."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000040 "#      Ueli Hugenschmidt contributed a patch for -fpsc"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000041 "#      Sam Kington supplied a patch to identify the initial indentation of"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000042 "#      entabbed code."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000043 "#      jonathan swartz supplied patches for:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000044 "#      * .../ pattern, which looks upwards from directory"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000045 "#      * --notidy, to be used in directories where we want to avoid"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000046 "#        accidentally tidying"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000047 "#      * prefilter and postfilter"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000048 "#      * iterations option"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000049 "#"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000050 "#      Many others have supplied key ideas, suggestions, and bug reports;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000051 "#        see the CHANGES file."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000052 "#"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000053 "############################################################"
